<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL RAISES DIESEL PRICE.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL RAISES DIESEL PRICE.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Wednesday it would raise its retail price for diesel in the Netherlands by 1.6 cents per litre with effect from September 27.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, it said.</p>
<p>From Friday the price of diesel at Shell's self-service stations will rise to 1.504 guilders per litre from 1.488 guilders.</p>
<p>The recommended prices for gasoline remain unchanged.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
